MODEL WATCH #57 — Tuesday, September 22, 2026

1. LODESTONE-R2 MINI
Distilled R2 at $0.80 / $3.20. On our reasoning set: 80.6 (R2: 94.8; Pelagic 2.5 capped: 88.9). Four times faster than R2. Cost per task $0.011, which makes it the cheapest model above 80 on reasoning.

  Model               Reasoning   Median latency   Cost/task
  Lodestone-R2           94.8         41s           $0.044
  Pelagic 2.5 (cap 800)  88.9         9s            $0.0079
  Lodestone-R2 Mini      80.6         10s           $0.011

2. COMMIT-PRICING TERMS, SIDE BY SIDE
Every provider now offers a prepay discount. The terms differ more than the percentages:

  Provider   Discount   Term        Transferable across models?   Refundable?
  Kestrel      15%      quarterly   no                            no
  Argent       12%      quarterly   yes                           no
  Nimbus       20%      annual      yes                           no
  Sable Labs   10%      annual      n/a (one model family)        no

With mid-tier prices falling 10–20% a month, an annual lock at 20% off is roughly break-even by December. Quarterly and transferable is the only version we would sign.

3. SABLE-3.1 MINI
Composite 76.0 (from 74.6). Same price. The head-to-head with Ferrite-70B: Mini is cheaper per token ($0.44 vs. $1.70 out) and 3 points worse on extraction. Pick by whether extraction accuracy or cost dominates your bill.

